<description>NN12689 Ver001: projected luminous trajectory for the 95% EARLIEST and MEDIAN (weighted mean) arrival. Straight line from 90 km to 20 km above the ground, between the points where the estimated gravity-curved path (through the 110 km point 32.168 N, 84.700 E at 2026-11-04 15:44:53.4 UTC) reaches those heights. Speeds are relative to the rotating Earth: 22.86 km/s down to 95 km, then constant deceleration 2.50 km/s^2 (255 g) to 3.0 km/s at 20 km. Luminous path length 95.8 km, duration 7.6 s. Estimated, not observed: the direction comes from the Meerkat e-mail analysis, there is no ablation/fragmentation model, ground taken at the WGS84 ellipsoid. The e-mail is confidential and the object unconfirmed: do not distribute.</description>
